  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Duns">Duns</ref> 8.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.4" corresp="#wit-q">Similiter debet Anglico Waliscus rectum facere.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.4" corresp="#wit-b">Gelice ðam Ænglisc sceal Wyliscan riht wyrcean.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-b">Similarly, the Englishman should work to implement the rights of the Welshman.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Diesem gleich soll der Engländer dem Wälschen Recht erfüllen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">In the same way the Englishman shall do justice to the Welshman.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">The Quadripartitus reverses this: ‘Similiter debet Anglico Waliscus rectum facere’ (the Welshman to the Englishman).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
